  <metadata>
    <name>Danube Cycle Path — Vienna to Budapest</name>
    <desc>Point-to-point route — 330 km / 205 mi cycling in Lower Austria to Hungary, Austria. Easy difficulty. Flat river paths, paved throughout. Best season: May – September. Drawn by hand in Utrecht, kept free for everyone, forever. No accounts, no tracking, no upsells — just two pairs of hands hoping this ride carries you somewhere good. If it does, that&apos;s the whole reason it exists. 🤍🚲</desc>
